  "response": "## Analyse\nJe vais améliorer le scoring avec TF-IDF simplifié en calculant la fréquence des mots et en ajoutant un bonus de position. J'intègre les learnings : stop words français, tests pour cas limites, et validation de l'interface existante.\n\n```python path: tools/summarize.py\nimport re\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom typing import List, Dict\n\n# Stop words français courants\nFRENCH_STOP_WORDS = {\n    'le', 'de', 'et', 'à', 'un', 'il', 'être', 'et', 'en', 'avoir', 'que', 'pour',\n    'dans', 'ce', 'son', 'une', 'sur', 'avec', 'ne', 'se', 'pas', 'tout', 'plus',\n    'par', 'grand', 'en', 'une', 'être', 'et', 'à', 'il', 'avoir', 'ne', 'je', 'son',\n    'que', 'se', 'qui', 'ce', 'dans', 'en', 'du', 'elle', 'au', 'de', 'le', 'un',\n    'à', 'être', 'et', 'en', 'avoir', 'que', 'pour', 'dans', 'ce', 'son', 'une',\n    'sur', 'avec', 'ne', 'se', 'pas', 'tout', 'plus', 'par', 'grand', 'en', 'une',\n    'être', 'et', 'à', 'il', 'avoir', 'ne', 'je', 'son', 'que', 'se', 'qui', 'ce',\n    'dans', 'en', 'du', 'elle', 'au', 'mais', 'ou', 'car', 'donc', 'or', 'ni', 'si',\n    'la', 'les', 'des', 'ces', 'ses', 'mes', 'tes', 'nos', 'vos', 'leurs'\n}\n\ndef extract_words(text: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Extract words from text, removing punctuation and stop words.\"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return []\n    \n    # Convert to lowercase and extract words\n    words = re.findall(r'\\b[a-zA-Zàâäéèêëïîôöùûüÿç]+\\b', text.lower())\n    \n    # Filter out stop words and short words\n    return [word for word in words if word not in FRENCH_STOP_WORDS and len(word) > 2]\n\ndef calculate_tf_scores(sentences: List[str]) -> Dict[str, float]:\n    \"\"\"Calculate term frequency scores for all words in the text.\"\"\"\n    if not sentences:\n        return {}\n    \n    # Extract all words from all sentences\n    all_words = []\n    for sentence in sentences:\n        all_words.extend(extract_words(sentence))\n    \n    if not all_words:\n        return {}\n    \n    # Calculate term frequencies\n    word_counts = Counter(all_words)\n    total_words = len(all_words)\n    \n    # Convert to relative frequencies\n    tf_scores = {word: count / total_words for word, count in word_counts.items()}\n    \n    return tf_scores\n\ndef score_sentence(sentence: str, tf_scores: Dict[str, float], position: int, total_sentences: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Score a sentence based on TF scores and position.\"\"\"\n    if not sentence or not tf_scores:\n        return 0.0\n    \n    words = extract_words(sentence)\n    if not words:\n        return 0.0\n    \n    # Calculate average TF score for words in sentence\n    word_scores = [tf_scores.get(word, 0.0) for word in words]\n    avg_tf_score = sum(word_scores) / len(word_scores) if word_scores else 0.0\n    \n    # Position bonus: +20% for first 3 sentences and last sentence\n    position_bonus = 1.0\n    if position <= 2 or position == total_sentences - 1:\n        position_bonus = 1.2\n    \n    return avg_tf_score * position_bonus\n\ndef summarize(text: str, max_sentences: int = 3) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Summarize text using TF-IDF scoring with position weighting.\n    \n    Args:\n        text: Input text to summarize\n        max_sentences: Maximum number of sentences in summary\n        \n    Returns:\n        Summary string\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text or not text.strip():\n        return \"\"\n    \n    # Split into sentences\n    sentences = re.split(r'[.!?]+', text.strip())\n    sentences = [s.strip() for s in sentences if s.strip()]\n    \n    if not sentences:\n        return \"\"\n    \n    if len(sentences) <= max_sentences:\n        return '. '.join(sentences) + '.'\n    \n    # Calculate TF scores for the entire text\n    tf_scores = calculate_tf_scores(sentences)\n    \n    if not tf_scores:\n        # Fallback: return first sentences if no meaningful words found\n        return '. '.join(sentences[:max_sentences]) + '.'\n    \n    # Score each sentence\n    sentence_scores = []\n    for i, sentence in enumerate(sentences):\n        score = score_sentence(sentence, tf_scores, i, len(sentences))\n        sentence_scores.append((score, i, sentence))\n    \n    # Sort by score (descending) and select top sentences\n    sentence_scores.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    selected_sentences = sentence_scores[:max_sentences]\n    \n    # Sort selected sentences by original position to maintain order\n    selected_sentences.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\n    \n    # Extract sentences and join\n    summary_sentences = [sentence for _, _, sentence in selected_sentences]\n    return '. '.join(summary_sentences) + '.'\n\n# Test function for validation\ndef test_summarize():\n    \"\"\"Test the summarize function with various cases.\"\"\"\n    \n    # Test normal case\n    text1 = \"Python est un langage de programmation. Il est très populaire. Python est facile à apprendre. Les développeurs aiment Python.\"\n    result1 = summarize(text1, 2)\n    print(f\"Test 1: {result1}\")\n    \n    # Test empty text\n    result2 = summarize(\"\", 3)\n    print(f\"Test 2 (empty): '{result2}'\")\n    \n    # Test single sentence\n    result3 = summarize(\"Une seule phrase.\", 3)\n    print(f\"Test 3 (single): {result3}\")\n    \n    # Test short text\n    result4 = summarize(\"Première phrase. Deuxième phrase.\", 3)\n    print(f\"Test 4 (short): {result4}\")\n    \n    print(\"All tests completed successfully!\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    test_summarize()\n```\n\n```bash\npython tools/summarize.py\n```",
